Slide 4 – Problem & Goals (Detailed)
- Problem: Need a scalable, responsive web app to engage users and prototype features quickly.
- Primary goals: Launch fast, support auth-gated dashboard features, automate builds/deploys.
- Secondary goals: Clean codebase, mobile-first UI, future-ready backend integration plan.

Slide 5 – Tech Stack & Rationale
- Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind: Modern DX, fast HMR, type safety, utility-first styling.
- Firebase Auth: Quick, reliable auth (email/password + Google) to unblock MVP.
- react-router-dom: Simple routing for public vs protected paths.
- DevOps: GitHub Actions + Netlify for predictable CI/CD and low-friction hosting.

Slide 6 – Architecture Overview
- Flow: Landing → Auth → Dashboard (tabs: Home, Education, Consultation, Event, Community, Profile).
- Separation: UI components in src/components, pages in src/pages, API stubs in api/.
- Future backend: Replace stubs with Supabase/Postgres or serverless functions.

Slide 7 – Feature Deep Dive
- Landing page: hero, features, stats, founders, pricing, testimonials, CTA, contact, footer.
- Auth: Email/password + Google via Firebase; redirects to /dashboard when logged in.
- Dashboard: Sidebar navigation; modules scaffolded for learning resources, events, consultations, posts, profile.

Slide 8 – UX, Accessibility, and Theming
- Dark/light theme persisted; motion/gradients mindful of readability; responsive layouts.
- Keyboard focus states; semantic sections; consistent contrast for text and interactive elements.

Slide 9 – DevOps Pipeline (CI)
- Workflow: .github/workflows/ci.yml triggered on push/PR.
- Steps: npm ci, lint, typecheck (tsc --noEmit), build (vite), upload dist artifact.
- Benefits: Catch errors early, reproducible builds, faster reviews.

Slide 10 – Continuous Deployment (CD)
- Netlify: netlify.toml (publish=dist, command=npm run build).
- Workflow: .github/workflows/deploy-netlify.yml on main; deploy via Netlify CLI.
- Secrets: NETLIFY_SITE_ID and NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN set in GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets.

Slide 11 – Security & Config Management
- Current: Firebase keys in code for MVP speed; move to Vite env (VITE_*) and GitHub secrets next.
- Harden: Limit public rules, enforce auth checks, consider RLS if using Supabase.
- CI hygiene: No secrets in logs; principle of least privilege.

Slide 12 – Performance & Optimization
- Vite build optimizations; code splitting by routes; minimal runtime deps on landing.
- Asset compression via Netlify; cache headers by default; image sizes constrained.
- Next: Lighthouse/Pagespeed audits; bundle analysis, lazy loading heavy modules.

Slide 13 – Testing Strategy (Now & Next)
- Now: Typecheck, lint, manual exploratory testing across flows.
- Next: Vitest + RTL for components; Playwright for auth + navigation; add to CI gates.

