Appendix – Common Q&A (Preparation Bank)
1) Why Vite + React + TypeScript?
   - Fast dev builds, strong typing to reduce bugs, broad ecosystem support for long-term maintainability.
2) Why Tailwind over CSS-in-JS?
   - Utility classes accelerate iteration; consistent design tokens; small runtime overhead, great for MVP.
3) Why Firebase Auth now and not custom backend?
   - Time-constrained MVP; secure, reliable auth; can migrate to Supabase/Auth or custom later without major UI changes.
4) How is dark mode managed?
   - App-level state persisted to localStorage; Landingpage receives darkMode and setDarkMode as props.
5) How are routes protected?
   - Public routes: /, /login, /signup. Dashboard routes check Firebase auth; unauthenticated users redirected to /.
6) What caused the initial build failure and how was it fixed?
   - Merge-conflict artifact and state mismatch; removed artifact, refactored Landingpage props; added typecheck in CI.
7) How does CI improve quality?
   - Ensures every push/PR passes lint, typecheck, and build before merge; artifacts allow reviewing build outputs.
8) How does CD work?
   - On push to main, GitHub Actions builds and deploys dist to Netlify with site/token secrets; netlify.toml configures publish.
9) Where are secrets stored?
   - GitHub repository secrets; not committed to the repo or echoed in logs. Firebase keys should migrate to VITE_* env.
10) How would you add a database now?
   - Prefer Supabase (Postgres + Auth + RLS). Create tables, migrate API stubs, add service layer, secure with RLS and policies.
11) How did you ensure responsiveness and accessibility?
   - Mobile-first grids, semantic HTML, focus states, sufficient contrast, and keyboard navigability.
12) How would you handle errors and monitoring?
   - Integrate Sentry for error and performance monitoring; alert on release regressions.
13) How would you secure the app further?
   - CSP headers, dependency scanning (Semgrep), role-based access control, strict auth/route guards.
14) How does the project scale?
   - Modular components, route-based code splitting, CI/CD for consistent releases, backend switchability via API layer.
15) What are the main risks and mitigations?
   - Secret leakage → repo secrets; build regressions → CI gates; vendor lock-in → API abstraction and migration plan.
16) How would you add tests without slowing velocity?
   - Start with high-value flows (auth, navigation), parallelize in CI, and adopt incremental coverage thresholds.
17) Why Netlify over alternatives?
   - Simple static hosting and preview deploys, good DX for Vite; can also support API functions if needed.
18) How to present performance improvements?
   - Use Lighthouse scores, bundle size reports, lazy loaded modules, and image optimization metrics.

